WEBVTT

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:05.277
Your benches may be solid, just under-equipped.

00:00:05.557 --> 00:00:08.276
Before you replace them, think about upgrading them.

00:00:08.876 --> 00:00:12.617
Replacing sound benches wastes money and disrupts production.

00:00:12.897 --> 00:00:17.279
Yet operators still need power, light and tool storage at the station.

00:00:17.879 --> 00:00:22.192
A retrofit adds a Link Uprighter onto the worktop you already have.

00:00:22.472 --> 00:00:28.058
Then you choose accessories for the task: a pegboard for hand tools, a bin rail for parts,

00:00:28.058 --> 00:00:33.209
a shelf for instruments, a power rail for equipment, and a light for detailed work.

00:00:33.489 --> 00:00:38.980
Each accessory hooks in, so you can start small and add more as you learn what the station needs.

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:43.764
The Furnisys Link Uprighter mounts on most existing workbenches.

00:00:44.044 --> 00:00:49.173
As a guide, the worktop should be about 6 inches wider than the frame,

00:00:49.173 --> 00:00:52.325
so a 48 inch frame needs a 54 inch worktop.

00:00:52.925 --> 00:00:56.859
Upgrade your benches one station at a time, without stopping the line.

00:00:57.139 --> 00:00:58.572
How old are your benches?

00:00:58.852 --> 00:01:03.401
Tell us in the comments, and next, start our accessories series with pegboards.

00:01:04.001 --> 00:01:08.246
Furnisys: complete workspace systems, planned around your process.

